This describes processes and executable files.

When a new process starts, it receives an initial message (although this
is optional if a debugger is attached, otherwise it is required). This
initial message is like any other message and can contain any bytes and/or
capabilities, and should contain at least one capability since otherwise
it cannot do any I/O and will be terminated autmoatically (unless there is
a debugger attached, in which case it cn be controlled by a debugger).

